# The rclone-manager-tests commit this repository's gate runs its browser
# e2e suite and its CLI smoke slice from. Moved by
# scripts/e2e/bump-tests-pin.sh, and the commit that moves it is itself
# gated against the new pin, so a bad bump cannot land unnoticed.
#
# Why this repository pins that one, and that one pins a build of this one:
# pinning the tests repository means a new or changed test cannot break
# unrelated in-flight work here until someone bumps this line, and the bump
# is itself gated. Pinning the product build over there means a release
# cannot silently change what those suites certify. Each is one line, in one
# file, reviewable on its own.
#
# At a794c38, read off rclone-manager-tests' merged main rather than a branch
# head, because a squash rewrites the head and the pin then names a commit in
# no history. It is exactly two commits past the sha this line held before, and
# both are #431's, so nothing unrelated arrives with the bump.
#
# Those are rclone-manager-tests#32 and rclone-manager-tests#33, which between
# them retire the two retention cases that recorded this binary's old note
# about FR-20 being unimplemented and replace them with one that asserts the
# note that replaces it. They are the specs half of #431; the product half is
# in the same branch as this bump, because either one alone leaves the gate
# red. The second of the two exists because I committed the first without
# staging two of its files, and that repository's own lockstep test caught it
# on main.
#
# It has moved once since, to 6520d0a, which is rclone-manager-tests#34: the
# archive case that follows rclone-manager#442 refusing a retention tier bound
# to an archive storage class at load. The two paragraphs above are about the
# bump that carried #431's specs and not about where this line points today,
# which is worth saying rather than leaving them to read as current. A pin
# header narrating a sha the pin no longer holds is the same defect #431 is
# about, in the file that was fixing it.
#
# This header used to narrate a deliberate hold at 9dfd6e3, waiting for #240's
# Suite B specs to have a product to run against. #240 landed, b2092a5 moved
# the sha to 57ef7b5, and nobody came back to the paragraph explaining the
# hold, so it went on describing a hold that had already ended. Worth a
# sentence rather than a silent delete: a comment nobody returns to is the same
# defect #431 is about, one file over.
#
# The hold was the arrangement working as designed, and the design has not
# changed. Specs are allowed to land over there ahead of the feature they
# describe, and this line is what stops them being enforced here until the
# feature arrives. Move the pin past a spec whose product change is not in this
# tree and that spec goes red; the gate catches it, which is the pin doing its
# job rather than a problem with it.
#
# It runs the other way too, and that half has no automation. rclone-manager-
# tests carries its own build-under-test.json naming a commit of THIS
# repository, and a spec landed ahead of its feature cannot go green over there
# until somebody moves it. Both of those commits are in that position right
# now: they need that file moved to #465's own merge commit.
#
# Moved to b3fe0f8, which is rclone-manager-tests#36, and read off that
# repository's merged main rather than off the branch, for the reason the
# paragraph about a794c38 above already gives. EPIC #536 gave every
# configuration read and write a "mode:" line on stderr saying which world
# its answer came from, and seventeen cases over there asserted stderr was
# empty. They now pin the sentence instead, with an absent matcher for the
# engine-attached form and a count so the case still promises nothing else
# is on that stream, which `empty` used to promise on its own. One more,
# g3, had a `daemon` description that now wraps onto three lines.
#
# The product half is in this same branch, because either one alone leaves a
# gate red: theirs was red against this pin until this line moved, and ours
# would go red the moment it did.
#
# That bump also carries one expectation that is not #536's. e57d26b landed
# retention/plain-retention-is-a-preview's stdout changes ahead of the pin
# and they have been waiting there since, so that case has two generations
# of ahead-of-pin expectation in it and both land together here.
#
# Still outstanding on their side, and still with no automation: their
# build-under-test.json names 3a489d2 of this repository and has to move to
# whatever commit this branch merges as, or #536's specs cannot go green
# over there.
#
# Moved to 0673850, rclone-manager-tests#40, off their merged main again. #555
# gives a read a third way to refuse, the engine at the address this host was
# given turning out to serve a different deployment, so the banner says three
# cases and g5 still pinned the sentence that said two. That is the pin
# noticing a product change rather than drift, which is the whole point of it.
#
# g3 needed nothing this time even though the same batch appended four lines to
# the banner's exit-code table, because g3 pins one line per command and a table
# row is not a command.
#
# Verified before the bump rather than after: a stamped build of this branch
# through RM_MODE=local runs the whole of Suite A green, 72 of 72. Their
# build-under-test.json names 1bed795 and still has to move to this branch's
# merge commit by hand, which is the half of the lockstep with no automation.
# Moved to 90c3bb1, rclone-manager-tests#46, read off their merged main and
# not off the branch, for the reason the paragraph about a794c38 above
# already gives. It is the specs half of #598: ten Suite B cases driving a
# failing Activity page, and four Suite A cases plus a usage line for the
# `activity` verb the same issue adds.
#
# This is the pin doing the thing the paragraphs above describe, in both
# directions at once. Seven of those ten cases fail against this
# repository's main as it stands, because they drive a mock scenario that
# does not exist there and assert on a diagnostic that is not written yet,
# so they were red over there against the old pin and go green here only
# together with the product change in this same branch. Four of the Suite A
# cases are the same shape one command over: there is no `activity` verb on
# main, so `global/g3-usage-lists-every-command` cannot see it.
#
# Verified before the bump rather than after, the way the note above asks:
# a stamped build of this branch through RM_MODE=local runs Suite A green,
# 76 of 76, and Suite B green against this branch's ui/shared, 198 of 198
# across the generic and small-window projects. The control matters as much
# as the pass: the same Suite B file run against a clean checkout of main
# fails 7 and passes 3, which is what makes it a test of the product rather
# than of the component.
#
# Moved again, to 41b0721, rclone-manager-tests#48, off their merged main.
# That one is the black-box half of the two CLI surfaces this branch adds
# beyond the durable activity read: `activity --follow` and `backup-set
# edit-hold`, both pinned by their REFUSAL rather than their happy path.
#
# Both refuse when nothing is serving this deployment, and for one reason:
# a live feed and an edit hold each live in the memory of the serving
# process and neither survives it, so with nothing serving there is no
# answer to give and a fallback would put a different feed, or an
# invented "not held", on screen looking exactly like an answer. Pinning
# the refusal is what stops a fallback being added later without anybody
# noticing. Their happy paths need a serving process, which is Suite C's
# arrangement, and their matrix rows say so rather than leaving the gap
# implicit.
#
# Verified before the bump, again: a stamped build of this branch through
# RM_MODE=local runs Suite A green, 78 of 78.
#
# Still outstanding on their side, and still with no automation: their
# build-under-test.json names 1bed795 of this repository and has to move to
# whatever commit this branch merges as.
#
# Moved to e7bf7a9, rclone-manager-tests#51 and #53, off their merged main
# and not off the branch, for the reason the paragraph about a794c38 above already
# gives. This one runs the other way round from most of the bumps above:
# their specs did not land ahead of a feature, they were pinning the old
# shape of three surfaces this branch changed on purpose, so five Suite B
# cases were red HERE against the old pin and go green with the bump.
#
# The run button lost "due". RunCycle walks every enabled backup set and
# skips only the disabled and the edit-held, so "due" named a filter that
# has never existed and the label was contradicting the tooltip printed
# beside it. Three of the five looked for the old name, including both
# version-mismatch cases, which are about management controls going off on
# an incompatible service and still are: only the name moved there.
#
# The set-detail header gained two controls. #597 built the per-set run for
# real, so "Run this backup set" sits beside the deployment-wide one and
# the case's own comment saying core has no per-set run had gone false;
# it enumerates both now and pins both tooltips, which is what #214 was
# about in the first place. #591 added CANCEL & EXIT EDIT MODE, asserted
# absent before edit mode opens and present after.
#
# The fifth is the opposite of the usual shape here: a limitation went
# away, so the spec asserting it was obsolete rather than wrong. #592's
# GET /ssh-keys is the read nothing had, so the wizard's managed-key panel
# lists what a deployment holds and can be saved. That case asserts the
# listing and a pick now, and keeps the half of #299 that still matters,
# that nothing fabricates an in-use count.
#
# #53 is the same discovery arriving one step late. The set-detail
# read-only case lists the controls that go off on an incompatible
# service, and #597's per-set run made that three of four, so it covers
# the fourth now. It reads the button's title back beside the disabled
# state rather than asserting the state alone, because that button is ALSO
# disabled when the set itself is disabled and a bare check could pass for
# a reason that has nothing to do with a version mismatch.
#
# Verified before the bump rather than after, the way the notes above ask.
# All five fail against this repository's main at 51f5f4f2 and pass against
# this branch, checked by pointing RM_UI_DIR at each checkout in turn, so
# they are a test of the product and not of the component. #53's assertion
# is checked both ways round too: that button is enabled under the default
# scenario and disabled under version-mismatch, so it is not trivially
# true. Suite B green at the new pin against this branch's ui/shared, 198
# of 198 across the generic and small-window projects.
#
# Still outstanding on their side, and still with no automation: their
# build-under-test.json names d2f4373 of this repository, which predates
# the activity verb, so seven of their Suite A cases from #46 and #48 are
# red over there until it moves to whatever commit this branch merges as.
# That is the same manual half the paragraphs above keep flagging, and it
# is not something a bump on this side can close.
TESTS_REPO_URL=https://github.com/spdrman/rclone-manager-tests.git
TESTS_REPO_SHA=e7bf7a9f3959abf8d42d35448afd30d1bac4aa09
